course: dictionary
lesson: 8658
title: Seasonal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you when something happens. Seasonal is one of them. It comes from season, one of the four parts of the year: spring, summer, autumn and winter. A seasonal thing happens, or is needed, only at one time of the year.
explain: Look at the clues in «Indian Ocean sailors timed their voyages with the seasonal monsoon winds». The sailors needed winds that blow at a certain time of year, so seasonal must mean linked to one time of the year. Try the swap: "the monsoon winds that come at a certain time of year" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: The word also shows up in everyday life. Shops have «seasonal sales» at Christmas, and doctors talk about «seasonal flu» in winter. In both, the clue is the time of year. Seasonal fruit is fruit that is ripe and fresh only at that time of year.
fact: Season means one of the four parts of the year: spring, summer, autumn and winter.
fact: «Seasonal» means happening or needed only at a certain season of the year.
fact: «Seasonal food» is food that is ripe and fresh at that time of year.
fact: «Seasonal work» is a job for only part of the year, like picking fruit or Christmas shop work.
fact: The South Asian monsoon is a seasonal reversal of winds: in summer, moist winds blow from the Indian Ocean onto India, and in winter, dry winds blow out from the land.
exercise: «Seasonal fruit» is fruit that is ripe and fresh only at a certain time of year. What does seasonal mean? | Happening every single day of the year | Very sweet and sticky | *Happening or needed only at a certain time of year | Made in a factory
exercise: Which of these is a seasonal job? | Living in the same house all your life | *Picking fruit for a few weeks each autumn | Teaching the same class every day of the year | Reading books at the library
exercise: «In summer, moist winds blow from the Indian Ocean onto India.» Find and copy one word that tells you a time of year. | winds | *summer | blow | Indian
test: Mia says «seasonal flu» means flu that happens all year round. Is she right? | Not sure, flu is a kind of fruit | *No, it happens only at a certain time of the year | Yes, it happens every single day | Yes, because flu is always the same
test: Why did sailors in «Indian Ocean sailors timed their voyages with the seasonal monsoon winds» plan their trips carefully? | Because seasonal means fast | Because the sea is blue | *Because the winds blow only at certain times of the year | Because the winds are always the same
exam: Which sentence uses seasonal correctly? | The seasonal ran across the road | My seasonal is brown with spots | Seasonal is a type of fish for dinner | *Shops have seasonal sales at Christmas
